import io

slot2_row = ("| §P.P5 Galway worst-case K-constant tightening, slot 2 — finer x-grid + heavy-compute extension; decisive measurement at log10 x = 5.5 distinguishing Galway-shape (c_emp = const) from Thread-7-shape (c_emp ~ √x/log²x). Two parallel paths in single session: (a) finer K-milestones at K_max=8000 across log10 x ∈ [4.0, 4.9]; (b) extend zero database to K_max=20000 via 12 parallel mpmath.zetazero workers, measure K_emp at log10 x ∈ {5.0, 5.3, 5.5}. "
"| EMPIRICAL (B-NEGATIVE-FOR-GALWAY-SHAPE / B-PARTIAL-POSITIVE-FOR-THREAD-7-SHAPE: at log10 x = 5.5 K=20000 budget exhausted with worst-case |err|=1.609; rigorous LB c_emp > 0.222; extrapolated c_emp ≈ 0.574 (under err ~ 1/√K) matches Thread-7-shape prediction c_emp_T7(5.5) = 0.596 within 4%; Galway-shape c_emp = const ≤ 0.222 REFUTED at log10 x = 5.5; σ_eff/σ_pred drift confirmed across 1.5 decades 0.72/0.79/0.88/1.0 at log10 x = 4.0/4.5/5.0/5.5) "
"| E (E1.5 + Thread 5 / S224 + Thread 7 / S195+S240+S244 + Galway 2004 / Buthe 2018 — Thread-7-shape extends to worst-case-of-N tail) "
"| Thread 10 commit step 2/3 (S435). Built `experiments/analytic/galway_constant/slot2_finegrid.py` (~165 lines: imports slot1 helpers, finer K-milestones every 250 above K=1000) and `experiments/analytic/galway_constant/slot2_extended.py` (~200 lines: extended-zeros loader combining `data/zeta_zeros_8000.txt` with `data/zeros_chunks_slot2/chunk_*.txt`, K-milestones every 1000 above K=5000 up to K_max=20000). Generated 12,000 new zeros (k=8001..20000 at 15 dps) via 12 parallel `mpmath.zetazero` workers in `data/zeros_chunks_slot2/` (per-zero cost 0.86s at k=8000s growing to 1.5s at k=19000s, ~25 min wall total). "
"**Slot 2 path-(a) — finer x-grid (10 anchors)**: c_emp at log10 x ∈ [4.0, 4.9] gave [0.147, 0.125, 0.106, 0.126, 0.138, 0.249, 0.168, >0.305 LB, >0.261 LB, >0.223 LB]; mean across 7 finite-K = 0.151 ± 0.044, range [0.106, 0.249]. σ_eff/σ_pred at K_emp regime = 0.71 ± 0.06 across 7 cells, consistent with slot 1's 0.80 ± 0.09 within 1σ. Single-decade range insufficient to distinguish shapes within sample variance (factor ~2× per anchor at N=30). "
